The directories under recorded/ hold texts that one container wrote each, on 2026-11-24.
The engine was Docker 29.8.2 on linux/arm64 with cgroup version 2, and its kernel mounted no version 1 hierarchy.
The image was perl@sha256:4a7dcd778e99d7766a245107a5ebbd2d55ac8355560deea633f1ee52768440ac.
The file command of a directory names the switches of its container.

cpu.max is /sys/fs/cgroup/cpu.max.
cpuset.cpus.effective is /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset.cpus.effective.
cgroup is /proc/self/cgroup.
status holds the two lines about the allowed processors from /proc/self/status of the cp command that copied it.
nproc is the output of nproc, and online is the output of getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN.
cpuinfo holds the processor lines of /proc/cpuinfo, which had the same text in every container.
The other lines of both files described the machine and no test read them.

The directories under constructed/ hold texts that nobody recorded.
The file source of such a directory names the documents that its texts follow.
